Day 33 (2026-10-26) - 3D models (STL) in the viewer (VersariteViewer 1.3)

1. Version 1.2.1 (user: there were downloads of 1.2 already):
   uEdition MViewVersion; release_notes_v1.2.0.md back to what 1.2 had,
   the later changes in release_notes_v1.2.1.md.
2. The user's STL viewer (C:\projects\lazarus_stl_viewer) fixed first:
   stencil / depth bits, the plane through the model's centre, the closed
   cut face (stencil count with the depth test off), Z up, smoothing by
   welded corners, display lists, ASCII files, drag & drop, Grid on / off.
3. uStlModel (new, imaging): reads binary (84 + 50 x count bytes) and
   ASCII STL ("vertex" lines); draws in software into a TBGRABitmap,
   orthographic, z-buffer, the STL viewer's colours and headlight
   (two-sided, Gouraud). Turn (around Z) and Tilt (elevation) as the
   viewer's glRotatef pair. Triangles in 1/16 pixel fixed point with a
   tie rule for shared edges (each pixel counted once). Section: per
   pixel, the part behind the plane left out; the cut face closed by
   counting, per pixel, the surfaces between the plane and the eye (odd =
   inside), the face at the plane's depth. Smoothing: corners welded by
   sorting quantised positions (once per model), faces within the
   level's angle averaged. Edges, grid, axes, the plane's frame as depth-
   tested lines. Models shared through a small cache (counted
   references: the decode worker and TMView use one copy). 180 000
   triangles: about 0.1 s at 1920 x 1080 (0.15 s with the edges).
4. uImageFormats: .stl listed. uMediaLoader.RenderStlImage: the start
   view (StlStartView) at twice the screen size (at most about 4K) with
   a screen-size copy, as qlFull; quick (screen size, qlScreen, the same
   full size) for TMView while turning.
5. uStlPanel (new, rendering): TStlSection, a panel section (uExtensions)
   with nine rows - Section, Flip side, Plane X, Plane Y, Plane position,
   Elevation, Smoothing, Grid, Edges; registered by TMView, rows only
   while a model is shown. uExtensions: TSectionRowKind (button, toggle,
   slider) and SliderPos / SetSliderPos / Wheel / ResetRow for sections;
   uFilterPanel: DrawPanelSlider / DrawPanelToggle (the filter rows'
   look, shared) and BarWidth; TMView.HandleFilterMouse drags, wheels and
   resets slider rows, and leaves out the second click of a double-click
   on a toggle.
6. TMView: StlNewImage (a model shown: its controls, the start view, the
   info line "N triangles   X x Y x Z"), cmdRotateBy / Left / Right turn
   the model (StlTurn; + = clockwise from above, R tap = 90 degrees), a
   change is drawn quickly at once (timer stage 1: many wheel notches
   give one picture) and sharp 400 ms later (stage 2); a better version
   of the file arriving then (window resized) is drawn as set, not the
   start view. The rotate mode's line says "model -60°". "Save image" of
   a model writes <name>.png.
7. Tests: TestStl (new, 25: reading binary / ASCII / refused, cache,
   drawing, closed cut face, panel rows). TestNavigation 153,
   TestExtensions 80. Checked under Wine: a cup and a 180 000-triangle
   sphere - section on, flipped (closed disc), plane tilted 60° (closed
   ellipse), turned in rotate mode, plane position dragged; both
   editions build.
8. Combine GIFs (user): uGifJoin (new, imaging) parses both GIFs to
   their frames (graphic control, descriptor, colour table, LZW data)
   and writes them unchanged into one GIF89a - no global table, each
   frame its own (its local one or its file's global one), the canvas
   the larger of the two with each animation centred, the first file's
   NETSCAPE2.0 loop. After each animation a clearing frame: the whole
   canvas, transparent (GifLzwEncode, a small LZW encoder), delay = the
   pause (0.5 s), disposal 2; the frame before it gets disposal 1, so
   the last picture stays through the pause and nothing shows through
   the next animation. Written as .part, then renamed. uTCFollow:
   PanelItems - the files under both panels' cursors (LP / LN, RP / RN;
   else path lines 9 / 10 and file lists 1 / 2, cursor 1007 / 1008).
   TMView.CombineGifs: both animated GIFs (2 frames or more), not the
   same (name or content, uFileMover.SameFileContent), into the folder
   shown as <left>_<right>.gif (_1 ...), then opened. Menu entry
   "Combine GIFs" below the dir preview, enabled only side by side with
   Total Commander running. TestGifJoin (new, 18). Not yet tried with a
   real Total Commander (none here).
9. A left drag turns a model in 3D (user): cmdPanBy -> TMView.StlOrbit
   while a model is shown (not in edit mode): left / right turns around
   the vertical axis, up / down tilts (elevation, -90 .. 90), half a
   degree per pixel as in the STL viewer. (The rotate-mode check: it
   did turn - the quick and the sharp picture line up.)
